## Action Classes

Single-purpose, invokable classes for complex business operations — use instead of fat services:

```php
<?php

declare(strict_types=1);

namespace App\Actions;

use App\Models\Post;
use App\Models\User;
use App\Events\PostPublished;
use Illuminate\Support\Facades\DB;

class PublishPost
{
    public function execute(Post $post, User $actor): Post
    {
        if ($post->published) {
            throw new \DomainException('Post is already published.');
        }

        return DB::transaction(function () use ($post, $actor) {
            $post->update(['published' => true, 'published_at' => now()]);
            PostPublished::dispatch($post);
            return $post->fresh();
        });
    }
}

// Usage in controller — one action per meaningful business operation
public function publish(Request $request, Post $post): PostResource
{
    $this->authorize('update', $post);
    $post = (new PublishPost)->execute($post, $request->user());
    return new PostResource($post);
}
```

