## N+1 Detection & Eager Loading

```php
// ALWAYS eager load relationships in list queries
// BAD — N+1 (one query per post to get author):
$posts = Post::all();
foreach ($posts as $post) { echo $post->author->name; }

// GOOD — 2 queries total:
$posts = Post::with('author', 'tags')->get();

// In controllers, explicitly define what to load per endpoint
public function index(): AnonymousResourceCollection
{
    $posts = Post::with(['author:id,name,avatar_url', 'tags:id,name'])
        ->published()
        ->orderByDesc('created_at')
        ->paginate(15);
    return PostResource::collection($posts);
}

// Detect N+1 in development — add to AppServiceProvider::boot()
if (app()->environment('local')) {
    \Illuminate\Database\Eloquent\Model::preventLazyLoading();
}
```

